// RUN: cir-opt %s -cir-offload-infer-kernel-param-noalias='host-facts=ipo host-facts-closed-tu=1 host-facts-bu=0 host-facts-subobjects=0' \
// RUN:   -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,CI
// RUN: cir-opt %s -cir-offload-infer-kernel-param-noalias='host-facts=ipo host-facts-closed-tu=1' \
// RUN:   -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,BU
// RUN: cir-opt %s -cir-offload-host-facts-host-ptr-ub=false \
// RUN:   -cir-offload-infer-kernel-param-noalias='host-facts=ipo host-facts-closed-tu=1' \
// RUN:   -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UBOFF
//
// Sub-buffer, ranged-accessor and host-pointer rules of the accessor identity
// (SYCLHostFacts::viewRange, sameMemory; the `$view` ghost links of
// SYCLPointsToModels.h). The cases are SYCL-MLIR's AccessorInformation::alias
// decision table plus the host-pointer cases. Two accessors of one storage
// are noalias only if the elements they may access are provably disjoint
// (constant offsets and ranges); an access outside an accessor's range is UB
// (SYCL 2020 PI 7613-7622, 7673-7678), so their accessed memory is disjoint
// even though both `ptr` parameters point into one storage (llvm.noalias is
// about the memory accessed). One case per kernel, launched from @case_<K>:
//  - SUBDIS / SUBOVL / SUBUNK: two sub-buffers of one 1024-element parent,
//    disjoint, overlapping, at an offset that is not a constant;
//  - RNGDIS / RNGOVL / RNGUNK / RNGNOOFF: two ranged accessors of one buffer;
//  - RNGSUB / RNGSUBOVL: a ranged accessor of a sub-buffer is composed with
//    the sub-buffer's offset ([512, 640)), vs the other sub-buffer / a ranged
//    accessor of the parent at [600, 700);
//  - SUBPARENT: a sub-buffer vs its parent's whole accessor: never;
//  - HOSTEQ: two buffers over the same host pointer: UB (PI 5358-5359), so
//    distinct storages with the default assumeSpecHostPtrUB; not with
//    -cir-offload-host-facts-host-ptr-ub=false (UBOFF);
//  - HOSTDIS / HOSTOVL: v and v + 512 (disjoint) or v + 256 (overlapping):
//    cir.ptr_stride makes v an array node, whose offsets are only known
//    modulo the element size, so neither is proven disjoint;
//  - HOSTFIELDS / HOSTFIELDSOVL: buffers over two member arrays of one
//    struct, by byte ranges (context-insensitive, one node, offsets 0 and 2048; with
//    subobjects the members are subobject nodes without an allocation site);
//  - USMHOST: a buffer over a USM pointer is the same memory as that pointer;
//  - LOCAL: a local accessor is not a candidate (no remark for L);
//  - MERGED: a buffer reference that may be the parent or a sub-buffer: the
//    whole view and the sub-buffer view unify, the range is not known.
//
// Generated by /localdisk3/kparasyr/ipo-aa/t25/tests/gen.py.

